RDS Multi-AZ: 60–120 s); writes fail until then. After: major, 18.6% errors. $562/month. `add db-replica (replica); connect db → db-replica`\n\n### Critical: lb goes down\n\n96.3% of requests failed while it lasted (peak 100.0%), p99 incl. failures up to 1.0 s.\n\nVerified fixes (re-ran the same incident):\n\n- **Run a standby lb** — A second load balancer that callers fail over to. After: ok. $36/month. `add lb-b (lb); connect users → lb-b; users: routing = failover; connect lb-b → api`\n\n### Critical: db turns slow (+250 ms)\n\n78.0% of requests failed while it lasted (peak 84.6%), p99 incl. failures up to 1.4 s. db spends 250 ms more on each request than its 10 ms of work, so each worker is busy 26× as long: it serves about 77 req/s instead of 2,000, under the 494 req/s it is offered, and sheds the rest. The incident is a gray failure of the component itself; slowness in the network in front of it would be `latencyMs` on the connection.\n\nVerified fixes (re-ran the same incident):\n\n- **Timeout + circuit breaker with fallback on api → db** — Give up quickly on the slow dependency and serve a degraded answer instead of making every answer wait for it. After: major, 7.6% errors. $0/month. `api: timeoutMs = 200, breaker = true, fallback = true`\n\n### Major: traffic surges 3× for 20 s\n\n21.2% of requests failed while it lasted (peak 33.3%), p99 incl. failures up to 1.1 s. Back within SLO 2 s after the surge ended.\n\nVerified fixes (re-ran the same incident):\n\n- **Scale api to 8 instances** — Double the fleet. After: ok. $292/month. `api: instances = 8`\n- **Size api up to M** — Bigger instance class: about twice the throughput. After: ok. $350/month. `api: tier = M`\n\n### Major: api fails 20% of requests\n\n18.8% of requests failed while it lasted (peak 20.0%), p99 incl. failures up to 1.0 s.\n\nVerified fixes (re-ran the same incident):\n\n- **2 retries with backoff on lb** — Most transient errors succeed on a second try; backoff with jitter spreads the extra load. After: ok, 0.70% errors. $0/month. `lb: retries = 2, retryPolicy = backoff`\n\n### Major: db fails 20% of requests\n\n18.6% of requests failed while it lasted (peak 20.0%), p99 incl. failures up to 1.0 s.\n\nVerified fixes (re-ran the same incident):\n\n- **2 retries with backoff on api** — Most transient errors succeed on a second try; backoff with jitter spreads the extra load. After: ok, 0.70% errors. $0/month. `api: retries = 2, retryPolicy = backoff`\n\n### Major: api turns slow (+250 ms)\n\n0.00% of requests failed while it lasted (peak 0.00%), p99 incl. failures up to 343 ms. api has no thread limit, so slow calls wait without holding a worker: it adds 250 ms to every answer but keeps serving.\n\n### OK: one api instance dies\n\nAbsorbed: users stayed within SLO (p99 peaked at 93 ms).\n\n### OK: load ramps past 1000 req/s\n\nSustains 1000 req/s within SLO — 2.0× the expected 500 req/s. api gives out first: Saturated at 101% — requests are queuing and latency is climbing steeply.\n\n---\nGenerated by Hindcast. Each incident: 10 s warm-up, fault at t = 10 s, cleared at t = 40 s, observed to t = 60 s. Results are directional — calibrate capacity, latency and price per component for real-system claims."
